# ️ Sakila Microservice Module Runbook

> **Purpose** — Step-by-step guide to scaffold a new microservice module in this project,
> following the exact same patterns used in `inventory-service` and `customer-service`.

---

## Table of Contents

1. [Architecture Overview](#1-architecture-overview)
2. [Import-Order Rule (Checkstyle)](#2-import-order-rule-checkstyle)
3. [Step 1 — Create the Maven Module](#3-step-1--create-the-maven-module)
4. [Step 2 — pom.xml Template](#4-step-2--pomxml-template)
5. [Step 3 — application.yaml Template](#5-step-3--applicationyaml-template)
6. [Step 4 — JPA Entity Checklist](#6-step-4--jpa-entity-checklist)
7. [Step 5 — DTO Records (Request / UpdateRequest / Response)](#7-step-5--dto-records)
8. [Step 6 — MapStruct Mapper Template](#8-step-6--mapstruct-mapper-template)
9. [Step 7 — JPA Repository Template](#9-step-7--jpa-repository-template)
10. [Step 8 — Exception Classes](#10-step-8--exception-classes)
11. [Step 9 — Config Classes](#11-step-9--config-classes)
12. [Step 10 — Service Interface Template](#12-step-10--service-interface-template)
13. [Step 11 — Service Implementation Template](#13-step-11--service-implementation-template)
14. [Step 12 — REST Controller Template](#14-step-12--rest-controller-template)
15. [Step 13 — Verify the Build](#15-step-13--verify-the-build)
16. [Quick-Start PowerShell Script](#16-quick-start-powershell-script)
17. [Naming Conventions Cheat Sheet](#17-naming-conventions-cheat-sheet)

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

```
<module-name>/
├── pom.xml
└── src/main/java/com/me/learning/parent/<modulename>/
    ├── <ModuleNameApplication>.java
    ├── config/
    │   ├── CacheConfig.java
    │   ├── LoggingInterceptor.java
    │   ├── OpenAPIConfig.java
    │   └── WebMvcConfig.java
    ├── controller/
    │   └── <Entity>Controller.java          (one per entity)
    ├── dto/
    │   ├── <Entity>Request.java             (create)
    │   ├── <Entity>UpdateRequest.java       (update / patch)
    │   └── <Entity>Response.java            (read)
    ├── entity/                              (or model/)
    │   └── <Entity>.java
    ├── exception/
    │   ├── DuplicateResourceException.java
    │   ├── GlobalExceptionHandler.java
    │   ├── InvalidRequestException.java
    │   ├── ResourceNotFoundException.java
    │   └── ServiceException.java
    ├── mapper/
    │   └── <Entity>Mapper.java              (one per entity)
    ├── repository/
    │   └── <Entity>Repository.java          (one per entity)
    └── service/
        ├── <Entity>Service.java             (interface)
        └── <Entity>ServiceImpl.java         (implementation)
```

---

## 2. Import-Order Rule (Checkstyle)

All files **must** follow this group order with a **blank line between each group**:

```
Group 1  java.*
Group 2  jakarta.*
Group 3  ch.*            (logback)
Group 4  net.*           (logstash)
Group 5  org.slf4j.*
Group 6  io.*            (swagger / openapi)
Group 7  org.apache.*
Group 8  org.assertj.*
Group 9  org.hibernate.*
Group 10 org.jspecify.*
Group 11 org.junit.*
Group 12 org.mapstruct.*
Group 13 org.mockito.*
Group 14 org.springframework.*
Group 15 lombok.*
Group 16 com.*
```

**Example — Controller:**
```java
import java.util.List;                          // Group 1

import jakarta.validation.Valid;                // Group 2

import io.swagger.v3.oas.annotations.*;         // Group 6

import org.springframework.http.*;              // Group 14
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;          // Group 15
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;

import com.me.learning.parent.xyz.*;            // Group 16
```

---

## 3. Step 1 — Create the Maven Module

```
mkdir <service-name>
cd <service-name>
mkdir -p src/main/java/com/me/learning/parent/<pkg>
mkdir -p src/main/resources
mkdir -p src/test/java/com/me/learning/parent/<pkg>
```

Copy `mvnw`, `mvnw.cmd`, `.mvn/` from any sibling module.

